WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.042
A distribution tells us how values are spread across ranges.

00:00:04.042 --> 00:00:11.327
The code places each number into a bin such as forty to forty-nine or fifty to fifty-nine.

00:00:11.327 --> 00:00:15.869
The number of hash marks represents how many values fall into that interval.

00:00:16.609 --> 00:00:23.396
This is the same basic idea as a histogram, just displayed with text instead of graphical bars.

00:00:23.396 --> 00:00:30.614
Look for where the values concentrate and whether the frequencies are balanced or uneven across the ranges.
